#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""powos units - everything installed or running on a host, with an owner, a purpose, limits and a clean way out.

A unit is anything that installs files or runs processes on a host: a PowOS app, a container, a system component, a
package dependency, a watcher/daemon. Each has a manifest, /etc/powos/units.d/<id>.json on its host (the phone's
Android side: /data/powos/units.d; the Mac: ~/.config/powos/units.d). Nothing is installed host-wide without one:
the install paths write it (powos app install, powos containers run, the deploy scripts, the system module) and
`powos units check` flags whatever has none. Dependencies belong INSIDE an app or a container, not on the host.

Usage:
  powos units [list] [--json [--check]] [--all]
                                        this host's units: status (running/asleep/stopped/installed), owner,
                                        memory and CPU, limits; orphans marked. --all: the repo's every host (units/)
  powos units show <id>                 one unit: everything its manifest says, what is running, its cgroup
  powos units check [--json]            drift: packages, files and processes no unit claims, processes of a unit with
                                        limits that run outside its cgroup, units whose files are gone. Exit 1 on drift
  powos units remove <id> [--dry-run] [--yes]
                                        uninstall it cleanly: shows the plan first (stop, packages, files, commands,
                                        what is kept); --dry-run stops there; without --yes it asks
  powos units register <manifest.json|->   add or replace a unit (validated); the install paths call this
  powos units unregister <id>           forget a unit (removes only its manifest, never what it installed)
  powos units enforce [<id>]            put each running unit with limits into a cgroup of its own with them
                                        (the containers' hybrid cgroups on the phone, cgroup v2 elsewhere)
  powos units baseline <id> --before YYYY-MM-DD [--owner O] [--purpose P]
                                        adopt what was installed before a date as one unit (the image, the user's
                                        own tools); what came after stays unclaimed for check to show
  powos units enter <id> [-- cmd...]    this process into the unit's cgroup, then exec cmd (a unit with "enter":
                                        "<user>" is delegated to that user by enforce, for what it starts unprivileged)
  powos units publish [--stdin [--failed REASON]]
                                        this host's units to the PowOS AI page (the powos-agents module's `unit`
                                        table); --stdin: another host's `list --json --check` (the Colima VM's);
                                        --failed: that host couldn't be read - its last rows, its _check "stale"

A manifest:
  {"id": "spacetimedb", "name": "SpacetimeDB", "kind": "service", "owner": "system:powos-deploy",
   "purpose": "the device's one SpacetimeDB server", "host": "phone",
   "packages": ["spacetimedb"], "files": ["/usr/lib/powos/apps/services/*.json"],
   "processes": [{"match": "spacetimedb-standalone start"}],          also {"pidfile": P, "tree": true},
                                                                       {"cgroup": NAME}, {"container": NAME}
   "limits": {"memory": "600m", "cpus": 2, "pids": 512},              or "unbounded": "why there is none"
   "autosleep": "never",                                               powos-sleep-common's key
   "remove": {"stop": ["cmd"], "commands": ["cmd"], "keep": ["/var/lib/powos/stdb"]},
   "orphan": true, "decide": "the question for the user"}             found with no clear owner: the user decides
   "ondemand": true                                                    installed only while used: absent isn't "missing"
   "enter": "powos"                                                    started by that user: enforce delegates its cgroup
  kind: app | service | container | system | package | watcher | compose | scratch.
  owner: app:<id> | agent:<role> | user | system:<what installed it>.

Hosts: phone (PowOS's root), phone-android (Android's side: Magisk, /data/powos, /data/local/tmp), colima (the Docker
VM), mac, powstation (the Docker containers, checked where docker runs), desktop. POWOS_UNITS_HOST overrides it,
POWOS_UNITS_DIR the directory. Docs: config/ai/context/capabilities.md (Units).
"""
